  "body": "## T-3353 \u2014 1919 Prairie's rear ranges quoined at their corners and banded in stone\n\nPiece 1 of **T-3338** (of T-3303, of T-1907). I split T-3338 this run. This piece builds the part of it the pictures settle. **T-3354** (piece 2, open) takes the rest: the rear ranges' roofs and place, read again.\n\n**What.** The 1919 programme plate draws 1919 Prairie's rear ranges with pale quoins up the corners where the flank steps out, and pale courses across the brick. Its match record calls these \"plainest of all\" its walls. Both ranges now carry:\n- **quoins** at each range's north-east corner (where its north wall meets the face it steps out on): long and short stones in turn, from grade to the 9.6 m wall top;\n- **the main block's three stone courses** (T-3305: under the principal sills, at the second floor, under the chamber sills), carried across both ranges' north walls and their stepped-out faces. They stop against the canted north bay and replace K03's brick string course there.\n\n**How.** K01 gets an additive `dressings` entry on a brick rear wing:\n- `belts` + `belt_sides`: stone courses laid as a main wall's belts, with the brick course dropped on those walls;\n- `quoins` at named corners (`south_front`, `south_rear`, `north_front`, `north_rear`): the first face's stone runs out over the arris so the two faces meet.\n\nIt refuses: a corner the wing doesn't have, a stone or course running through a light, a course on a wall the wing doesn't have, an unknown key, a frame wing, and out-of-bounds sizes. Every other house is **byte-identical**: k01, k12, k13, k16 and draft emits were all re-run, and only 1919's GLB changed.\n\n**Provenance.** That the corners are quoined and the courses run on comes from the plate. The stones' 0.55/0.3 m lengths, 0.35 m courses, 0.03 m projection and the courses' lines (the main block's, carried on) are RECONSTRUCTED. They are recorded in the new liberty `L-k01-1919-range-dressings-3353`, and the record's note is INFERRED.\n\n**Image gate.** Both match records were re-rendered on the new GLB, and both stay `differs`. In the programme plate's record, \"the rear ranges' stone\" is now `fixed`. A new `open` item covers the canted bay's own corners, which the plate draws dark and doesn't resolve. In the 1913 record the item stays `not shown`, and its text now names this work.\n\n**Why not the pinnacled dormers (T-3354).** Both the programme plate and the 1912 Blue Book plate (read at full size, 3-4\u00d7 crops) show the small pinnacled dormers on a slate slope facing the street-side camera, with the steep gables standing *behind* them. The ranges as built have north-facing gable ends abutting at u -7. That leaves no slope for the dormers, and K01 refuses a gabled projection on a wing's gable end. So the dormers wait on the ranges' roofs being read again against all three Gatlin plates. Projecting the record through the programme camera puts the plate's gable apexes about 27 px right and 20-60 px higher than the built ones. That reading is written into the liberty and into T-3354's title.\n\n**Visible-progress rule.** Visible: from the programme plate's camera, the ranges' corners and bands now read pale where the plate's do (side-by-side in `docs/RESEARCH/photo-match/marshall_field_jr_house_1919_prairie/`).\n\n## Verification (runner, foreground)\n- `tools/check.sh --part 1/4 \u2026 4/4`: all four **PASS** on the final tree. Part 4 first failed only because the new step had no isolation row. I measured it with `measure_step_isolation.mjs --tool` (it writes nothing in-tree) and re-ran part 4: PASS.\n- **A gate step reported a missing module:** check.sh says `numpy (numpy) is not installed, so 9 step(s) below stand on a banked reading`. Those 9 steps were not taken on this runner. CI's own check runs them.\n- `tools/test_k01_wing_dressings.py` (new, in check.sh): PASS. It holds the two quoin instances, their course counts, limestone proud on both faces at each corner from grade to the wall top, and 8 refusals.\n- Smoke, `--published`: **part 3 mobile 390\u00d7780 PASS** (107/0), **part 3 desktop 1280\u00d7800 PASS**, **part 1 desktop PASS** (95/0, scaffold). Zero page errors in all three. Part 14 was not run: it is priced at 9 m 55 s against the 10 m cap.\n- `node tools/changelog-entries.mjs --check`: OK (`changelog.d/T-3353.json`).\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
